dsmr-email-encabulator (1.0-15) trixie; urgency=low

  * Pull in dsmr-localfirst (>= 1.0-1) for system-first recipient routing on
    hybrid domains, and raise the dsmr-qmail-run floor to >= 1.0-10 for the
    run-script wiring that activates it.
  * Add a documentation tree under /usr/share/doc, split by architecture
    profile: doc/common/ holds the architecture-neutral core (base qmail
    notes, dev log, research, tasks, DKIM, packaging workflow, common index)
    that carries into any stack metapackage; doc/ root holds the full-stack
    profile docs (vpopmail/dovecot notes, upgrade notes, reference manual,
    profile index).  The stack documentation now lives in the repository
    rather than an out-of-tree scratch area.
  * Install the texinfo reference manual into /usr/share/info and register it
    with doc-base so documentation catalogs index it.
  * Add an external mail client configuration guide (IMAP reading and SMTP
    submission, for both system accounts and vpopmail accounts).

